-- title:
--   Ultralimits of positive functionals, limit GNS representations and the subrepresentation generated by an element
-- statement:
--   Throughout, Hilbert spaces are complex, inner products $\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle$ are linear in the second variable, $B(H)$ is the $C^*$-algebra of bounded operators on $H$, and $\mathbb{C}$ carries the partial order $z\le w\iff w-z\in[0,\infty)$. A positive linear functional on an ordered algebra $A$ is a $\mathbb{C}$-linear map $f:A\to\mathbb{C}$ with $f(a)\le f(b)$ whenever $a\le b$. For an ultrafilter $\omega$ on a set $I$, $\lim_{i\to\omega}$ denotes the limit along $\omega$.
--
--   1. **Ultralimits of bounded families.** If $(z_i)_{i\in I}$ are complex numbers with $|z_i|\le R$ for all $i$, then $\lim_{i\to\omega}z_i$ exists (the closed disc of radius $R$ is compact), and it is unique.
--
--   2. **Ultralimit of functionals.** Let $A$ be a $C^*$-algebra, not necessarily unital, equipped with a partial order, and let $(f_i)_{i\in I}$ be positive linear functionals on $A$ with $|f_i(a)|\le\|a\|$ for all $i$ and $a$. Then
--
--      $$
--      f_\omega(a)=\lim_{i\to\omega}f_i(a)\qquad(a\in A)
--      $$
--
--      defines a positive linear functional $f_\omega$ on $A$.
--
--   3. **Vector functionals.** Let $A$ be a unital $C^*$-algebra with its usual order, $\pi:A\to B(H)$ a unital $*$-homomorphism and $\xi\in H$. The vector functional $\omega_{\pi,\xi}(a)=\langle\xi,\pi(a)\xi\rangle$ is positive, and $|\omega_{\pi,\xi}(a)|\le\|a\|$ for all $a$ when $\|\xi\|\le 1$.
--
--   4. **Limit representation.** Let $(H_i,\pi_i,\xi_i)_{i\in I}$ be a family of Hilbert spaces $H_i$, unital $*$-homomorphisms $\pi_i:A\to B(H_i)$ and vectors $\xi_i\in H_i$ with $\|\xi_i\|\le 1$, and let $\omega$ be an ultrafilter on $I$. The limit functional is the ultralimit of the vector functionals of item 3,
--
--      $$
--      \varphi_\omega(a)=\lim_{i\to\omega}\langle\xi_i,\pi_i(a)\xi_i\rangle .
--      $$
--
--      The limit Hilbert space $H_\omega$ and the limit representation $\pi_\omega:A\to B(H_\omega)$ are the GNS construction of $\varphi_\omega$: $H_\omega$ is the Hilbert-space completion of $A$ for the semi-inner product $\langle a,b\rangle_\omega=\varphi_\omega(a^*b)$, and $\pi_\omega(a)$ is the continuous extension of left multiplication $b\mapsto ab$. Thus $\pi_\omega$ is a unital $*$-homomorphism.
--
--   5. **Subrepresentation generated by an element.** For a unital $*$-homomorphism $\pi:A\to B(H)$ and $v\in A$, let
--
--      $$
--      K_v=\overline{\operatorname{span}}\,\{\,\pi(a)\pi(v)y \;:\; a\in A,\ y\in H\,\}\subseteq H .
--      $$
--
--      This closed subspace is invariant under every $\pi(a)$, and $a\mapsto\pi(a)|_{K_v}$ is a unital $*$-homomorphism $A\to B(K_v)$: the subrepresentation of $\pi$ on the smallest closed invariant subspace containing $\pi(v)H$.
--
--   The limit representation turns a family of representations with chosen vectors into a single representation that keeps asymptotic information. In the surrounding development it is shown that $\pi_\omega(a)=0$ whenever $\|\pi_i(a)\|\to0$ along $\omega$, and that $\pi_\omega(a)\neq0$ whenever there is $\delta>0$ with $\|\pi_i(a)\xi_i\|\ge\delta$ for $\omega$-almost every $i$. The restriction to $K_v$ is used to pass to the part of a representation generated by the range of $\pi(v)$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Lean names: `exists_complex_ultralimit`, `ultraValue` (a chosen limit) with `tendsto_ultraValue`, `ultraPositive`, `vectorPositive` with `vectorPositive_norm_le`, `limitFunctional`, `LimitHilbert` (Mathlib's `GNS` space of the functional), `limitRep` (Mathlib's `gnsStarAlgHom`), `generatedRange` (the `topologicalClosure` of the span, with a completeness instance), `generatedRange_invariant`, `rangeRestriction` and `rangeRestriction_apply`. Positive functionals are Mathlib's positive linear maps into the complex numbers with `ComplexOrder`. In items 1 and 2 the partial order on $A$ is arbitrary; in items 3 and 4 it is any order making $A$ a star-ordered ring, which for a $C^*$-algebra is the usual one; item 5 uses no order. Representations are unital star-algebra homomorphisms into the continuous linear operators.
